# Canonical identities for `git shortlog`, `git log --author` and GitHub's
# contributor graph.
#
# Two entries, both cleaning up history rather than changing it:
#
#   * the maintainer's name is spelled two ways across the log, because the
#     configured user.name changed at some point;
#   * `Test User <test@example.local>` is not a person. A test that shelled out
#     to git without scoping its environment wrote that identity into this
#     repository's own .git/config and authored real commits with it. The
#     incident is described in AGENTS.md, and `internal/git/gittest` now fails
#     any package whose tests change the repository's git configuration.
Michaël de Vries <vriesdemichael@gmail.com> Michael de Vries <vriesdemichael@gmail.com>
Michaël de Vries <vriesdemichael@gmail.com> Test User <test@example.local>
